For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Write each word in lower case, as in running text, unless it is a name or an acronym. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

SPOKE: support consisting of a radial member of a wheel joining the hub to the rim.
STEP: any maneuver made as part of progress toward a goal.
STROKE: (sports) the act of swinging or striking at a ball with a club or racket or bat or cue or hand.
SUPERPOSITION: (geology) the deposition of one geological stratum on another.
TAG: a label written or printed on paper, cardboard, or plastic that is attached to something to indicate its owner, nature, price.
